    <string name="audit_prompt">Please review the source code of the Bekon Agent app %1$s installed on my phone. This is exactly the installed version (tag v%1$s).

Code: %2$s
Archive: %3$s

Key files (direct plain-text links, pinned to the tag):
%4$s

If you cannot open links, say so and ask me to download the archive and upload it to you.

Answer only from the actual code, with file:line references. No generic checklists, no guessing. If you could not read a file, say which one explicitly.

Check:
1) what data leaves the device, where to and when (every network endpoint and tunnel);
2) how permissions are used (accessibility, screen capture, notifications) and whether anything is excessive;
3) how agent access is checked (owner approval, session token) and whether it can be bypassed;
4) whether Stop, Pause and Read-only really cut access.
Summary, briefly: what looks fine and what raises questions.</string>
